  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "php_hash_unserialize_spec",
    "file": "php-src/ext/hash/hash.c",
    "description": "HashContext unserialization accepts attacker-controlled internal state fields without validating cross-field consistency. For xxh32, only `memsize < 32` is checked in `php_hash_xxh32_unserialize`, but `total_len_32` and related state can be forged so that XXH32_update takes the large-length memcpy path and computes an out-of-bounds source pointer/size (seen as read size 0xFFFFFFFC). The crash manifests in XXH32_update/XXH_memcpy during `hash_update`, but the root cause is incomplete validation during hash state unserialization.",
    "conditions": "Input must unserialize to a `HashContext` object (via fuzzer-unserializehash harness) using algorithm `xxH32` with crafted serialized state array values. After unserialize, calling `hash_update($ctx, $data)` with a small/normal string triggers use of the corrupted xxh32 state. Because unserialize did not reject inconsistent internal fields, update performs an invalid large memcpy read past the provided data buffer, causing ASan heap-buffer-overflow."
  },
